AArch64 TicketLock3
(* Ticket lock (Promising-ARM PLDI'19 §7 "TL"): take a ticket with LDADDA
   on `next`, spin with LDAR on `owner` until it equals the ticket, critical
   section increments a counter, release with STLR of ticket+1 to `owner`.
   Three threads each take the lock once.
   Property: counter = 3 in every final state. Expected: Always.
   Proved for all layouts and any number N of threads (N + 1 < 2^32):
   `TicketLock.ticket_counter_envG`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/TicketLockPublic.lean).
   Open: liveness over the executable certification. `Live.Ticket.TicketLive fuel`
   (weak and memory fairness, the Stage 3 statement; Promising/LiveTicket.lean)
   for fuel >= 1. Its promise-free fragment is proved (below).
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t next`, `owner`, `counter`, the width of every access)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. Proved from the runner's exact configuration
   (declarations and initial memory included): `ticket_counter_envG_runner`, concrete
   `ticket_counter_envG_runner_concrete3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64TicketRunner.lean).
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (each access resolves as
   at `decls = {}`): `ticket_counter_envG_runner_noFault`, concrete
   `ticket_counter_envG_runner_noFault_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64NoFaultDLocks.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `ticket_counter_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `ticket_counter_envG_runner_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64FaultFreeFixed.lean).
   Proved both at once (safety and fault freedom, at the union of their
   hypotheses): `ticket_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree`, concrete
   `ticket_counter_envG_runner_safe_faultFree_concreteN 3` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/RunnerSafeFFA64.lean).
   Proved (LIVEPF): the promise-free fragment on a valid layout,
   `Live.TicketPF.ticket_live_pf [ValidLayout (layout tkWorker)] : TicketLivePF fuel`,
   concrete `ticket_live_pf_concrete` (Promising/LiveTicketPF.lean); `TicketLive`
   (promises allowed) stays open. On an invalid layout one thread can spin forever
   (KNOWN_GAPS.md, "Liveness (LIVEPF)"). *)
# flags: -sym
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t next=0; uint32_t owner=0; uint32_t counter=0;
0:X0=next; 0:X1=owner; 0:X2=counter;
1:X0=next; 1:X1=owner; 1:X2=counter;
2:X0=next; 2:X1=owner; 2:X2=counter;
}
threads { P0: worker done; P1: worker done; P2: worker done; }
code {
worker:
  MOV W6,#1
  LDADDA W6,W3,[X0]
spin:
  LDAR W4,[X1]
  CMP W4,W3
  B.NE spin
  LDR W5,[X2]
  ADD W5,W5,#1
  STR W5,[X2]
  ADD W4,W3,#1
  STLR W4,[X1]
  B done
done:
}
forall [counter]=3
